   "source": [
    "### 3.5 History Depth Split\n",
    "\n",
    "Fair completeness alone does not guarantee enough history for seasonal modeling. Prophet's seasonal decomposition needs to separate a genuine annual pattern from random noise, which requires observing that pattern repeat across multiple cycles. Standard time series practice treats two full seasonal cycles as a minimum and three as the preferred threshold for a reliable fit, since three complete years gives 36 monthly observations, enough to distinguish a real recurring shape from coincidence. Market commodity pairs are therefore split by both completeness and years of active history, into a smaller, deep history group suited to Prophet, and a broader, shorter history group suited to the LSTM or simpler baselines, which do not depend on multi year seasonality to function."
   ]
  },
