   "source": [
    "### 3.8 Outlier Event Verification\n",
    "\n",
    "An IQR flag is a screening signal, not proof of a data error. Each flagged observation is reviewed against its unit-standardized value, duplicate status, market history, neighboring months, and source record. An observation is marked as a data-error candidate only when it has an invalid or inconsistent unit, a duplicate or malformed record, or an implausible isolated jump unsupported by nearby observations. A geographically concentrated and internally consistent spike is retained as a possible genuine market event, even when its cause cannot be confirmed from the WFP file alone. These retained events are important to the early-warning use case and should be corroborated with market, drought, conflict, or supply-chain records when those sources are available."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "416466b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.9 Outlier Persistence Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "An IQR flag alone cannot distinguish a genuine market shift, where prices settle at a new level and stay there, from a transient spike that reverts, or a data entry error that appears once and never repeats. Each flagged outlier is classified by comparing the price level in the months immediately after the flagged date against the baseline level in the months immediately before it. If the new level persists, it is treated as a genuine shift worth investigating further. If it reverts close to baseline, it is treated as a transient spike, a real but temporary event. This same logic is the direct precursor to the residual based anomaly detection layer planned for the final system, since both rely on comparing actual behavior against a recent baseline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bd389af2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def classify_outlier(row, data, window=2):\n",
    "    series = data[(data[\"market\"] == row[\"market\"]) & (data[\"commodity\"] == row[\"commodity\"])].sort_values(\"date\")\n",
    "    match = series[series[\"date\"] == row[\"date\"]]\n",
    "    if match.empty:\n",
    "        return \"unknown\"\n",
    "    pos = series.index.get_loc(match.index[0])\n",
    "    before = series.iloc[max(0, pos - window):pos][\"price_per_kg\"]\n",
    "    after = series.iloc[pos + 1: pos + 1 + window][\"price_per_kg\"]\n",
    "    if before.empty or after.empty:\n",
    "        return \"insufficient surrounding data\"\n",
    "    baseline = before.mean()\n",
    "    reverted = abs(after.mean() - baseline) < abs(row[\"price_per_kg\"] - baseline) * 0.5\n",
    "    return \"transient spike\" if reverted else \"persistent shift\"\n",
    "\n",
    "outliers_by_commodity[\"classification\"] = outliers_by_commodity.apply(\n",
    "    lambda row: classify_outlier(row, modeling_data), axis=1\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
