   "source": [
    "### 3.14 Data Preparation Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Data Preparation addressed the structural issues surfaced during cleaning. Retail price is the primary modeling target and wholesale observations remain available in `retail_raw` for future comparison. Price observations were explicitly aggregated to one market-commodity-month grain, while daily NASA POWER rainfall and temperature were aggregated to monthly frequency before integration. Commodity labels were kept distinct rather than merged, since WFP records different products, such as raw grain and flour, under separate labels that carry genuinely different price behavior. Completeness was measured against each market commodity pair's own active reporting window rather than the full dataset span, since most series only began consistent reporting in late 2023, and a fixed span measurement unfairly penalizes commodities and markets that started later. Units were standardized to a common price per kilogram basis, with weight based units, including gram denominations initially missed, converted correctly, and genuinely non weight units, such as liters and countable items, left unconverted and excluded from weight based analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "Rainfall and temperature lags are retained as candidate features and will be selected through time-series validation. IQR flags were reviewed as possible data errors or genuine market events; flagged values were retained unless a later source check identifies a clear data-quality defect. The resulting Price-Weather Data Integration table is split chronologically into train, validation, and test sets to support honest monthly backtesting."
   ]
  }
